---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Stardew Valley" description="My Stardew Valley guides and resources">
  <div class="gaming-detail-page">
    <section class="gaming-hero gaming-hero--detail">
      <p class="home-kicker">Cosy game notes</p>
      <h1>Stardew Valley</h1>
      <p>
        My ultimate cosy game. I can happily spend hours tending my farm, fishing by the river, exploring the mines, or wandering through Pelican Town. With the mods I use, there is always something new to discover.
      </p>
          <div class="garden-hero-flower garden-hero-flower--herb" aria-hidden="true">
        <img src="/images/flowers/pressed-herb.svg" alt="" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="gaming-note-panel">
      <p>
        The resources below are for my own reference and ease of access. I have either created them myself, or sourced them elsewhere and included a note for the creator or owner.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="gaming-resource-panel" aria-labelledby="stardew-resources-heading">
      <div class="gaming-resource-panel__header">
        <p class="home-card__eyebrow">References</p>
        <h2 id="stardew-resources-heading">Stardew resources</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="gaming-tabs">
        <div class="gaming-tab-list" role="tablist" aria-label="Stardew Valley resources">
          <button class="gaming-tab-button active" id="mods-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-controls="mods" aria-selected="true" onclick="showTab('mods')">
            Current Mods
          </button>
          <button class="gaming-tab-button" id="museum-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-controls="museum" aria-selected="true" onclick="showTab('museum')">
            Museum layout
          </button>
          <button class="gaming-tab-button" id="fish-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-controls="fish" aria-selected="false" onclick="showTab('fish')">
            Fish guide
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="gaming-tab-content">
          <div class="gaming-tab-pane show active" id="mods" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="mods-tab">
            <p>The number of available mods for Stardew is insane and continues to keep growing. I usually pick a good number of design change mods that impact the way the buildings look, as well as any character avatar mods or updates to relationship mechanics.</p>
            <p>However, because of how many mods there are, I've changed my tactic of choosing individual mods (which then becomes a huge maintenance task), I've started using modpacks, with the most recent I'm trying; </p>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <a href="https://www.curseforge.com/stardewvalley/modpacks/dew-it-all" target="_blank">
                  Dew It All
                </a>
                by
                <a href="https://www.curseforge.com/members/kehaan/projects" target="_blank">
                  Kehaan
                </a>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="gaming-tab-pane" id="museum" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="museum-tab">
            <div class="image-layout">
              <p>Source: <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/StardewValleyExpanded/comments/1hfag51/my_museum_layout/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">u/FoxgloveAndFireflies</a></p>
              <img 
                src="/images/gaming/museum-layout.png" 
                alt="Museum layout reference for Stardew Valley"
              />
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="gaming-tab-pane" id="fish" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="fish-tab">
            <div class="image-layout">
              <p>Source: <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/StardewValley/comments/7rekkf/updated_visual_fish_by_season/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">u/Fynzou</a></p>
              <img 
                src="/images/gaming/fish-guide.png" 
                alt="Visual fish guide for Stardew Valley"
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    function showTab(tabId) {
      // Hide all tab panes before showing the selected resource.
      const tabPanes = document.querySelectorAll('.gaming-tab-pane');
      tabPanes.forEach((pane) => {
        pane.classList.remove('show', 'active');
      });
      
      // Remove active states from all tab buttons.
      const tabButtons = document.querySelectorAll('.gaming-tab-button');
      tabButtons.forEach((button) => {
        button.classList.remove('active');
        button.setAttribute('aria-selected', 'false');
      });
      
      // Show selected tab pane.
      const selectedPane = document.getElementById(tabId);
      if (selectedPane) {
        selectedPane.classList.add('show', 'active');
      }
      
      // Add active state to the selected tab button.
      const selectedButton = document.getElementById(tabId + '-tab');
      if (selectedButton) {
        selectedButton.classList.add('active');
        selectedButton.setAttribute('aria-selected', 'true');
      }
    }
  </script>
</BaseLayout>

